expr main <([know, knows, knew, wonder, wonders, wondering, ask, asks, asked, decide, decided, deciding, unsure, sure, see, check, depends, determine, debate, debating] weather [(or not), (to go), (to stay), (to leave)]), (weather)>

let message "Did you mean `whether`?"
let description "To introduce a choice, use `whether`; `weather` is about the sky."
let kind "Spelling"
let becomes "whether"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "We don't know weather or not it works." "We don't know whether or not it works."
test "I wonder weather or not to leave." "I wonder whether or not to leave."
test "Decide weather to go." "Decide whether to go."
test "Ask weather to stay." "Ask whether to stay."
test "She asked weather or not it rains." "She asked whether or not it rains."
test "It depends weather or not you try." "It depends whether or not you try."
test "They debate weather to go." "They debate whether to go."
test "Unsure weather to stay." "Unsure whether to stay."
test "He knows weather or not it is true." "He knows whether or not it is true."
test "Check weather or not it works." "Check whether or not it works."
test "I'm unsure weather to leave." "I'm unsure whether to leave."
test "We decided weather or not to go." "We decided whether or not to go."
test "See weather or not it helps." "See whether or not it helps."
test "They are deciding weather to stay." "They are deciding whether to stay."
test "I know weather or not he did." "I know whether or not he did."

allows "The weather is nice."
allows "Bad weather or not, we ride."
allows "The weather today is warm."
allows "What's the weather?"
allows "Whether or not you agree, we go."
allows "I know the weather will turn."
